# This session, as `systemd --user` knows it.
#
# `graphical-session.target` refuses to be started by hand: what a desktop is meant to
# bring is a target of its own bound to it, which is this one. Until something does,
# nothing keyed to a graphical session runs -- the desktop portal is
# `Requisite=graphical-session.target` and fails outright, and `xdg-user-dirs.service`
# wants `graphical-session-pre.target`, which is where a person's Downloads folder
# comes from.
#
# rikka-compositor starts this where it publishes the session's environment, and on the
# way out starts rikka-session-shutdown.target, which is what ends it -- stopping this
# one would not, and that file says why. What is `PartOf=graphical-session.target` --
# the portal and its backends, most of all -- then comes down with the session that
# started it rather than outliving it and answering the next one about a screen that is
# gone.

[Unit]
Description=Rikka session
Documentation=man:systemd.special(7)
BindsTo=graphical-session.target
Wants=graphical-session-pre.target
After=graphical-session-pre.target
Wants=xdg-desktop-autostart.target
Before=xdg-desktop-autostart.target
Wants=rikka-replay.service
Wants=rikka-remote.service
